[Odd polarization degree]\label{thm:odd}
Let $M$ be ample on $A$ and suppose that $D=\chi(M)$ is odd. For each $d\ge1$, a nonempty open of smooth curves in $|M^{3d}|$ has relative stable rank
\[
 r_d=\begin{cases}
 9Dd^2-1,&d\text{ odd},\\
 9Dd^2-3+f_A,&d\text{ even}.
 \end{cases}
\]
The corresponding full curve defect $g(C)-f_C$ is $2-f_A$ in odd degree and $2(2-f_A)$ in even degree. These are the generic ranks of the complete linear systems.

\label{lem:theta-jets}
In the smooth-theta case the following hold.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Every twist of $2\Theta$ is generated by global sections. The system $|2\Theta|$ separates distinct $x,y$ if $y\ne-x$.
\item The system $|3\Theta|$ separates three distinct values and separates second jets at every point. In particular it is very ample.
\item For distinct $P,Q$, the evaluation on their two first jets is onto except possibly when
\begin{equation}\label{eq:badpairs}
 2P+Q\in\Theta\quad\text{and}\quad P+2Q\in\Theta.
\end{equation}
For a fixed nonzero $g$, only finitely many pairs $(P,P+g)$ satisfy \eqref{eq:badpairs}.
\item If $n\ge4$, $|n\Theta|$ separates any two first jets and any three distinct values.
\end{enumerate}

[Principal norm sources]\label{lem:principal-source}
Let $M$ be ample on $A$ and put $D=\chi(M)$. Suppose either that $D$ is odd or that $A$ is ordinary. There are a principally polarized surface $(B,\Theta_B)$ and a finite \'etale isogeny $\phi:B\to A$ of degree $D$ such that
\[
 \phi^*M\equiv\OO_B(D\Theta_B),\qquad
 \Nm_\phi\OO_B(\Theta_B)\equiv M.
\]
There is also an ample bundle $N$ on $A^\vee$ with
\begin{equation}\label{eq:dual-pol}
 \chi(N)=D,\qquad\lambda_N=D\lambda_M^{-1}.
\end{equation}
